---
import NavigationIcon from "../components/NavigationIcon.astro";
import PublicLayout from "../layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
import Waitlist from "../components/Waitlist.astro";
import JournalArt from "../components/JournalArt.astro";
import ApproachComparison from "../components/ApproachComparison.astro";
import FitGuide from "../components/FitGuide.astro";
import DataBoundaries from "../components/DataBoundaries.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<PublicLayout title="Why Lore — Project memory for your existing coding agent" description="Decide whether Lore fits your workflow: existing coding agents, local history, reviewable project knowledge, and Git-based sharing.">
 <section class="section page-intro field-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why Lore</p><h1>When Lore fits your workflow.</h1><p class="hero-desc">For an existing coding agent: searchable local history, knowledge you can correct, and conventions you can review in Git.</p><a class="button button-primary" href={`${base}docs/install/`}>Choose your setup →</a></div><JournalArt name="satchel" size={120} eager /></section>
 <nav class="page-sections section" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#pillars"><NavigationIcon name="app" /><span>Is it a fit?</span></a><a href="#landscape"><NavigationIcon name="workflow" /><span>Compare approaches</span></a><a href="#cost"><NavigationIcon name="activity" /><span>Data &amp; costs</span></a><a href="#portability"><NavigationIcon name="bookmark" /><span>What’s available</span></a></nav>
 <section class="section" id="pillars"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Does this sound familiar?</h2></div><dl class="capabilities"><div><dt><NavigationIcon name="chat" /><span>Continue work across sessions</span></dt><dd>Find earlier work in Sessions; keep project decisions available across conversations.</dd></div><div><dt><NavigationIcon name="bookmark" /><span>Inspect what was learned</span></dt><dd>Check a rule’s source, correct it in Knowledge, and review the <code>.lore.md</code> diff.</dd></div><div><dt><NavigationIcon name="branch" /><span>Carry conventions through Git</span></dt><dd>Review shared conventions in the same pull request as your code.</dd></div></dl></section>
 <section class="section fit-section" id="landscape"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Choose the approach that matches your workflow.</h2><p>Choose your situation, then compare the tradeoffs below.</p></div>
 <FitGuide />
 <ApproachComparison /><p class="small muted">Official documentation linked above was checked on 27 October 2026. These products can overlap; the rows describe starting points and do not imply that any tool lacks other capabilities.</p></section>
 <section class="section" id="context-engine"><span id="depth" class="fragment-anchor" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="section-heading"><h2>Storage is only one part of the workflow.</h2><p>Lore records history, distills older working context, and curates project knowledge. What reaches a request is selected within scope and context limits. Your agent can use recall to look up details beyond that material.</p></div><a class="text-link icon-link" href={`${base}docs/memory/`}><span class="link-label">Understand stored history and current context</span> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
 <section class="section" id="cost"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Know the extra work before a long session.</h2><p>Distillation, curation, and conversation imports can make model calls. Provider pricing, model choices, and configuration affect their cost. Inspect recorded estimates in the local app and compare them with your provider’s actual usage.</p></div><DataBoundaries compact /><a class="text-link icon-link" href={`${base}docs/data-and-costs/`}><span class="link-label">See the data flow, telemetry choice, and cost views</span> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
 <section class="section" id="portability"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Three ways of keeping and sharing memory.</h2></div><dl class="capabilities"><div><dt><NavigationIcon name="app" /><span>Local Lore · Available now</span></dt><dd>Recorded sessions, context management, recall, and curated project knowledge through supported clients.</dd></div><div><dt><NavigationIcon name="branch" /><span>Git-based sharing · Available now</span></dt><dd>Commit and review <code>.lore.md</code>. It shares the knowledge file, not the full conversation database.</dd></div><div><dt><NavigationIcon name="people" /><span>Folk Lore · Early access</span></dt><dd>The upcoming hosted team experience for continuous sharing. Joining the list expresses interest; it does not enable sync.</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link icon-link" href={`${base}docs/team-memory/`}><span class="link-label">Review the current Git workflow</span> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Try a result you can inspect.</h2><p>Use a disposable project to check recording, inspect extracted knowledge and try recall as separate milestones.</p></div><a class="button button-primary" href={`${base}docs/example/`}>Try the sample workflow →</a><p><a href={`${base}docs/benchmark/`}>Read the historical benchmark and its limitations</a></p></section>
 <span id="team" class="fragment-anchor" aria-hidden="true"></span><Waitlist />
</PublicLayout>
